"""Terms of the MESBG rules manual (2024) that the vanilla/Battle Companies definitions refer to but do not define.

`headings` are section titles in the manual (every occurrence is included, parentheses and rule-example numbers ignored);
`paragraphs` are (regex, following-paragraphs) pairs for terms the manual only defines inline; `aliases` are other
spellings used by the definitions files (synonyms only: a related concept is a separate term, linked with `see`);
`first` keeps only the first N paragraphs of the headings' text (an extraction boundary: it only stops the text of the
next chapter from leaking in); `synth` marks long rule chapters whose brief entry is written by the curating agent in
tools/glossary_summaries.json (the build reports the ones still missing and falls back to the verbatim text). Entries
are brief reminders, not rule chapters. The text itself is extracted from the (local, gitignored) rulebook by
tools/build_glossary.py.
"""

T = lambda name, category, headings=(), aliases=(), paragraphs=(), see=(), first=None, synth=False: dict(  # noqa: E731
    name=name, category=category, headings=list(headings), aliases=list(aliases), paragraphs=list(paragraphs),
    see=list(see), first=first, synth=synth)

